# Every file under cli-tests is compared byte for byte, so git must not touch a
# single one of them.
#
# Some fixtures have CRLF endings on purpose (replace-keeps-crlf-line-endings)
# and some have no final newline on purpose
# (remove-last-block-invents-final-newline). Those bytes ARE the test. With
# git's end of line conversion in play, a checkout on another machine, or any
# core.autocrlf setting, would rewrite them and the cases would pass while
# testing nothing.
#
# -text turns off all end of line conversion for this directory.
* -text
